today's wildflowers are charvi jessica  and angelina from dallas texas  these girls made headlines when they  came up with a virtual  tutoring program called tutor scope  the non-profit helps kids and their  parents  keep up with the school work during the  pandemic i'd love to welcome them  charvi jessica angelina are you there  okay tell us about tutor  so we started tutorscope back in march  of 2020  when the pandemic was starting and um  schools were beginning to go virtual  and with that it became apparent that  student-to-teacher interactions would be  affected because  you can't really just walk up to a  teacher's desk to ask them a question um  in a virtual setting  so i thought what if we could have  student tutors  teaching other students virtually so i  asked angelina and jessica to join me  and they were so excited within two  weeks we had our entire website and  system up and running for  students to actually um start getting  tutored  and now we have over 22 tutors  that are spread out all across the  united states including ohio  texas and even arizona  i mean this is amazing i have to ask the  next question which is  do you think that the psychology of also  young people  seeing other young people because here's  me in home school  um it literally and my kids don't look  at me  like the teacher you know i'm their  parent and  you know do you think that that am i the  only parent that feels this way  do kids feel this way is there a kid  adult dynamic what do you think  there's definitely this component of us  being closer to the curriculum  um so kids are able to just like kind of  connect with us a little more  it's just very stressful right now for  everyone  and so um we kind of also just help with  the workload and the stress that parents  have right now  and then also um like decreasing the  amount of frustration that can be  happening with like  having to become the teachers during  this time because that's  that's just a new thing for a lot of  parents jessica  how do you feel about teaching kids you  can do it in your own state or  other states can sign up to learn with  you guys right  yeah exactly we'll tutor any kid no  matter  what city or state they're in and really  our main objective ever since  we founded this organization was to have  everything  be completely free of cost to the  student so  that has definitely allowed us to be  accessible to a lot of kids  we've had about 250 students with us and  you know over 500 have registered  um so and they're all you know from  elementary school to high school  so it's been a really great experience  and angelina  like what's next for your non-profit do  you plan on expanding  everybody's like coming from even other  countries what's the plan yes  of course of course um well like you've  already mentioned  we've actually been getting application  from countries like canada india or even  russia  and we hope to continue creating a  bigger impact on a global scale to every  child in need  angelina do you ever see parents like me  on the floor  like just flipped out yeah i mean  we see you know first-hand parents and  everyone in general they're just  so stressed because of all the changes  that we've had to go through  so we um hope to you know we read  parents of that stress as well i can't  thank you enough  i mean this is so hard this really is  do you feel like you are connecting with  these younger people  and really bringing like alleviation  of all this stress yeah that's  definitely what we're hoping to  accomplish you know  i mean as angelina was saying this  pandemic has just brought on  so many new changes and stresses and  um what our goal is is to kind of just  create that student-to-student  interaction  that you'd normally get in school so you  know before  we study for upcoming tests during lunch  and things like that  so we just really kind of want to create  that same dynamic and same environment  with tudor scope  i can't thank you enough as a parent  for all adults out there you know i  think that kids are going to  see you and actually  honestly behave themselves a little bit  better and trust in the process  a little bit more thank you no thank you  thank you  actually and i just want to donate five  thousand dollars  to you guys and your organization and  your company  just to spend on whatever way you see  fit for  the growth and development of the tudor  scope program because  honestly and i'm gonna match it with  another five thousand so that's ten  thousand  to you guys thank you so much oh my god  thank you so much  you all deserve cake so much worse  so welcome you all deserve capes go out  there and fly and save  us thank you charvey jessica  and angelina tutor scope visit our  website for more information and how  you can sign up for tudor scope  you
 

